Ravi Mehrotra, A. Nandakumar and Tanvir Kaur
The group agreed with the need for testing the efficacy of vaccines(s) against HPV in order to assess its 
impact on cervical cancer. The group discussed the type of vaccines that would be ideal for India, the 
difficulties in their testing; the age & sex groups on which the trial should be carried out; dosage schedule; 
existing organizations through which the trial/ intervention programme could possibly be carried out; 
ethical issues associated with a vaccine trial; costing and cost-effectiveness of a HPV vaccine programme; 
strategies for prevention of cervical cancer; end-points for a vaccine trial, possible sites for a vaccine trial; 
etc. Questions were put forward to the meeting participants and upon extensive discussions and debate 
